					<h1 class="title" title="Honeymoon Places in India">Honeymoon Places in India</h1>
					<div class="entry-content">
<p>After a long chain of rituals in marriages honeymoon is an opportunity to relax and spend time with your beloved husband. <b>Honeymoon</b> is also an important period for during that period you two closer as you both get the time devoted only to each other and you got to understand each other in better way. This is helpful in starting a new journey of your life. India has myriad <b>Honeymoon destinations</b> that are very romantic and will give you memories that are cherished all through your life. Honeymoon in India is altogether an exclusive experience which can be treasured. Let your <b>Honeymoon in India</b> be written with golden ink with varied exclusive and exciting honeymoon destinations here.

<p>India is a beautiful country adorned by rivers, seas, Oceans and Mountains making it a perfect Honeymoon destination. Taj Mahal at Agra, Goa, Cochin, Delhi, Jaipur, Kerala, Nainital, Ooty, Shimla, Kashmir, Darjeeling, Coorg, Kodaikanal, Shimla, Andaman and Nicobar, Khujaraho, Mussorie, Kullu-Manali......the list of <b>Honeymoon destinations in India</b> is endless. Every place has its own characteristics; thus Indian Honeymoon destinations are loved by the couples from all over the world.</p>

<p>India's topographical variations range from the beaches in Orissa, Kerala, Goa and Andaman Islands to Hills in many states in India.</p>
 
<p><b>Goan beaches</b> like Anjuna Beach, Arambol Beach, Agonda Beach, Baga Beach, Dona Paula Beach, and the Palom beach are wonderful place to enjoy sun and sand. These beaches are visited by hoard of tourists and also makes Goa <b>popular Honeymoon destination</b>.</p>
 
<p>The experience of <b>backwaters of Kerala</b> makes the state perfect honeymoon destination. The scenic beauty and serene environment presents a wonderful romantic environment. Also Kerala has popular Alappuzha Beach, Bekal Beach, Kovalam beach, Marari Beach and the Varkala Beach. </p>

<p>The group of islands in Bay of Bengal, Andaman and the Nicobar has numerous beaches. It is a <b>famous Honeymoon place</b> because of the golden sandy beaches. Radhanagar Beach, Harminder Bay Beach, Karmatang Beach, and the Ramnagar Beach with leather black turtles welcome honeymooners.</p>

<p><b>Kullu</b> and <b>Manali</b> are most popular <b>beautiful hillstations</b> in the lap of Lower Himalayas. The snow capped mountains; lush green surrounding and flourishing orchard is a popular <b>Honeymoon destination for adventure sport lover</b> couples. The hot water springs, waterfalls apart from dotted beautiful temples and monastery are worth visiting.</p>

<p>The picturesque beaches of Digha, Shankarpur, Junput, Bakkhali, Frazergunj and Sagardwip in West Bengal are also regarded as <b>prominent honeymoon beaches</b>. </p>


<p>If you want to sense royalty in your honeymoon the <b>royal Honeymoon destinations of India</b> are for you both.  Udaipur, the <b>city of lakes in Rajasthan</b> is definitely tops the list. The stunning palaces and placid lakes of Udaipur presents great romantic environment. The divine view at Pichola Lake, City Palace, Sajjangarh Fort, and boating in lakes are attraction for all. </p>

<p><b>Jodhpur</b> is also known as Blue city because the buildings here are coloured blue. The royal vista of the city includes the gorgeous <b>Umaid Bhawan Palace, impressive Mehrangarh Fort and Jaswant Thada</b> besides other structures has placed Jodhpur on the map of top Honeymoon destinations of India.</p>

<p>The exotic sculptures in the temples of Khajuraho are perfectly <b>royal retreat for romantic honeymoon in India</b>. The craftsmanship of UNESCO World Heritage Site is excellent.</p>

